# 7. LOCAL SMS PARSER

Implement a dedicated, testable SMS parsing engine.

The parser must identify supported payment messages using:

- Sender ID.
- Known message structure.
- Transaction type.
- Amount.
- Sender/customer number.
- Transaction ID.
- Timestamp.
- Reference, fee, commission and balance when available.

Parsing must happen locally.

The app must not forward unrelated SMS messages to the backend.

Support the following initial message specifications. These are initial parser patterns supplied for development, not a guarantee that every provider uses these formats in every situation.

## 7.1 bKash

Expected sender ID: `bKash`

### A. Personal account — Send Money received

```text
You have received Tk [Amount] from [Sender 11-Digit Number]. Ref [Reference]. Fee Tk 0.00. Balance Tk [New Balance]. TrxID [Transaction ID] at [DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM]
```

Transaction type:

`SEND_MONEY_RECEIVED`

Extract:

- Amount
- Sender number
- Reference
- Fee
- Balance
- Transaction ID
- Transaction time

### B. Personal account — Agent Cash-In received

```text
Cash In Tk [Amount] from [Agent 11-Digit Number] successful. Fee Tk 0.00. Balance Tk [New Balance]. TrxID [Transaction ID] at [DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM]. Download App: bka.sh
```

Transaction type:

`AGENT_CASH_IN_RECEIVED`

The sender number represents the agent, not necessarily the customer.

### C. Agent account — Customer Cash-Out received

```text
You have received Cash Out Tk [Amount] from [Customer 11-Digit Number]. Comm Tk [Commission]. Balance Tk [New Balance]. TrxID [Transaction ID] at [DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM].
```

Transaction type:

`CUSTOMER_CASH_OUT_RECEIVED`

