# 11. PAYMENT MATCHING RULES

The app must preserve transaction semantics so the backend can match events correctly.

### Send Money received

- Sender number represents the customer.
- Backend can compare it with the customer number entered during checkout.

### Agent Cash-In received

- Sender number represents the agent/uddokta.
- It is not the student's/customer's number.
- Never substitute the agent number for the customer number.
- Amount alone must not identify a student.
- Unmatched or ambiguous events remain pending/manual review.

### Customer Cash-Out received

- The customer number may be available in the notification.
- Backend validates the registered wallet/account configuration before using it for matching.

### Duplicate and ambiguous events

- Preserve transaction IDs.
- Do not submit repeated events as separate new transactions.
- Use idempotency and local duplicate checks as an optimization.
- Backend remains authoritative for duplicate prevention.
- Do not change a pending event to successful based only on an amount match.

